%erg v1
Title: make test scripts default to build/erg to avoid stale vendored binary runs
Created: 2026-05-04
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-05-04T19:25Z claude created — celebrate sweep found repeated default-binary anti-pattern across shell tests

--- body ---
## Context

During celebrate sweep after ticket verification hardening, we found the
same anti-pattern in seven test scripts:

- tests/test_close.sh
- tests/test_init_uninstall.sh
- tests/test_migrate.sh
- tests/test_nextid.sh
- tests/test_ready.sh
- tests/test_update.sh
- tests/test_validate.sh

All default to `tickets/tools/go/erg` when `ERG_BIN` is unset. This can
run a stale committed bootstrap binary when scripts are executed directly,
instead of the freshly built `build/erg` used by `make test`.

## Actions

1. Update all shell tests to default `ERG` to `build/erg`.
2. Keep `ERG_BIN` override support for explicit runners.
3. Ensure `make test` still passes unchanged.
4. Verify direct invocation of each script uses the rebuilt binary path.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] No test script defaults to `tickets/tools/go/erg`.
- [ ] All test scripts default to `build/erg`.
- [ ] `make test` and direct script runs remain green.
